id: VS-02
name: Risk Identification
short_description: Produce a structured, linked, owned risk inventory that is actionable
  and portfolio-ready.
owner: null
stakeholders:
- Risk Owners, BU leadership, Risk Function, Change teams, Procurement, Security
triggers:
- Periodic cycle, new initiative, post-incident review, regulatory request, emerging
  risk flagged (VS-01).
inputs:
- Context packs (VS-01), workshop outputs, incident learnings (VS-09), org/service
  maps, supplier lists.
entry_criteria: ''
key_activities:
- 1) Execute identification methods (workshops, interviews, data mining)
- 2) Draft cause–event–impact statements
- 3) Classify to taxonomy
- 4) Assign owners and reviewers
- 5) Link to objectives/KPIs, services/assets, suppliers
- 6) Identify duplicates and consolidate
- 7) Triage materiality/urgency
- 8) Queue for assessment (VS-03)
decisions_and_gates: []
outputs:
- Normalised risk records
- ownership
- dependency links
- triage status
- assessment backlog entries.
exit_criteria: ''
metrics: 'Flow: time from identification to triage; throughput of risks normalised;
  WIP of unowned risks.<br>Performance: % risks meeting quality standard; duplication
  rate.<br>Risk: proportion of material risks lacking assessment schedule.'
source_file: docs\value-architecture\value-streams\VS-02-risk-identification.md
last_updated: '2026-02-01T13:44:06.265547Z'
